// backlog #14 — apps/api/tsconfig.json excludes **/*.spec.ts and
// **/*.test.ts from typecheck, so a spec constructing a service with a
// wrong/missing dependency (review #455, teams.archive.spec.ts:159 — fixed
// in this PR) or any other type error inside a spec is never caught by
// `pnpm typecheck`. This project extends the same compilerOptions and
// points ONLY at spec/test files.
//
// Deliberately NOT wired into `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm test`, or CI yet:
// measured baseline on 2026-08-17 was 307 errors across 77 files — see the
// PR body for the full count and the decision not to fix all of them (and
// not to flip this into a blocking gate) in this PR. Run it by hand —
// `pnpm --filter @crm/api typecheck:specs` — to see the current count and
// work through it incrementally; each spec fixed shrinks the remaining set.
// Flip this into the blocking `typecheck` script (or CI) only once the
// count is at/near zero — enabling it before that would redden a
// currently-green main, which is backwards (git-policy.md's push-order rule).
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "dist"],
  "include": ["src/**/*.spec.ts", "src/**/*.test.ts"]
}
